{
  // §64's room-aware audio, as data. `HOUSE-00388`.
  //
  // Three parts. **Zones** give every cell its ambient bed and its gain; the beds are
  // shared rather than one per room, because room tone is a bed and ninety-six of them
  // would be ninety-six samples nobody could tell apart. **Emitters** are §62.6's own
  // sounds, placed from §12.5's stacks and the mechanical room -- that is what makes them
  // coherent rather than sprinkled. **Transmission** is §64.3's table, once, as the
  // classes every portal's `soundLoss` is derived from.
  //
  // The conversion is `loss = 1 - 10^(-dB/20)`: a 16 dB door passes 15.8 % of the
  // amplitude, so it loses 84.2 % of it, and that fraction is what a portal row carries.
  // §15.7 rule 6 checks every portal against its class, so the two cannot drift.
  "schema": "cna-house/audio/1",
